    "title": "Lab 3.2",
    "section": "Data interpretation",
    "text": "Data interpretation\nThere is a clear positive relationship between Fresh and Milk spending. Customers who spend more on Fresh products generally also spend more on Milk products.\nSpending behavior differs by customer Channel. Horeca and Retail customers show different spending patterns, which suggests that customer type influences how products are purchased.\nMost customers concentrate at lower to moderate spending levels, while a small number of customers show much higher spending. These high-spending customers appear as visible outliers in the chart, even without using log-scaled axes."
